
title: Thalia
---
<<declare $thaliaReceivedGem = false>>
<<declare $thaliaPositiveInteractionUnlocked = false>>
<<declare $thaliaPositiveInteractionSeen = false>>
<<declare $metThalia = false>>
<<declare $towerInvestigationStarted = false>>
<<declare $towerInvestigationComplete = false>>
<<declare $towerPeopleSpokenTo = 0>>
<<declare $spokeToVillagerAboutTower = false>>
<<if $metThalia == false>>
    Thalia: Well, well... What have we here?
    {$playerName}: Who said that?
    Thalia: Behind you.
    {$playerName}: What?!
    Thalia: Hah! You should have seen your face.
    Thalia: Relax. If I wanted to hurt you, you wouldn't have heard me coming.
    {$playerName}: Who are you?
    Thalia: Depends who's asking.
    {$playerName}: Someone who's trying to figure out where they are.
    Thalia: Hm. Then I suppose we're in the same boat.
    Thalia: Name's Thalia. Though most people know me as the Ghost.
    {$playerName}: The Ghost?
    Thalia: What can I say? I've got a talent for being somewhere I'm not supposed to be.
    Thalia: Guards never see me coming, and by the time they notice something's missing...
    Thalia: Well, I'm already gone.
    {$playerName}: So you're a thief?
    Thalia: Such an ugly word.
    Thalia: I prefer someone with exceptionally good borrowing skills.
    {$playerName}: Right...
    Thalia: Anyway, I was minding my own business gathering supplies around town.
    Thalia: Nothing particularly exciting.
    Thalia: Then, next thing I know, I'm waking up in a graveyard.
    {$playerName}: A graveyard?
    Thalia: Yep. Surrounded by tombstones.
    Thalia: Almost makes you wonder if the Ghost finally became an actual ghost.
    {$playerName}: You don't remember how you got there?
    Thalia: Not a thing.
    Thalia: And trust me, I don't like forgetting things.
    Thalia: Especially when I wake up somewhere I didn't intend to be.
    {$playerName}: You're not the only one.
    {$playerName}: Other people seem to have woken up here too.
    Thalia: So I've noticed.
    Thalia: Funny thing is, nobody seems to remember exactly what happened.
    {$playerName}: Do you think it has something to do with the tower?
    Thalia: Maybe.
    Thalia: I've heard a few people mention it.
    Thalia: But rumours are about as useful as a lock without a key.
    Thalia: We need something more concrete.
    {$playerName}: What are you suggesting?
    Thalia: Simple.
    Thalia: You talk to the people around here.
    Thalia: Find out what they remember before waking up on this island.
    Thalia: Three different people should give us somewhere to start.
    {$playerName}: Why don't you ask them yourself?
    Thalia: Because people tend to get nervous when the Ghost starts asking questions.
    Thalia: Besides, you're new here. People might be more willing to talk to you.
    {$playerName}: So you want me to do the talking?
    Thalia: Exactly! See? You're catching on.
    -> Agree to help
        {$playerName}: Alright. I'll see what I can find out.
        Thalia: Good. Speak to three people and come back to me.
        Thalia: I want to know what they remember about the tower and how they ended up here.
        <<set $towerInvestigationStarted = true>>
        <<start_quest QuestManager "investigate_tower">>
        Thalia: And try not to get yourself killed.
        Thalia: I'd hate to have another ghost wandering around here.
    -> Not right now
        {$playerName}: I've got other things to deal with first.
        Thalia: Suit yourself.
        Thalia: But if you want answers, you'll need to start asking questions.
    <<set $metThalia = true>>
<<else>>
    <<jump ThaliaReturn>>
<<endif>>
===

title: ThaliaReturn
---
<<if $towerInvestigationComplete == true>>
    <<jump ThaliaRelationship>>
<<elseif $towerInvestigationStarted == false>>
    Thalia: Well, look who decided to show up again.
    Thalia: Changed your mind about helping me investigate?
    -> Accept the investigation
        {$playerName}: Alright. I'll help you find out what happened.
        Thalia: Excellent!
        Thalia: I knew you'd come around eventually.
        Thalia: Speak to three people and find out what they remember.
        <<set $towerInvestigationStarted = true>>
        <<start_quest QuestManager "investigate_tower">>
        Thalia: Come back when you've learned something useful.
    -> Leave
        {$playerName}: Maybe later.
        Thalia: Don't take too long.
        Thalia: I'd rather not spend eternity on this floating rock.
<<elseif $towerPeopleSpokenTo >= 3 && $foundTeleporter == true && $spokeToVillagerAboutTower == true>>
    Thalia: There you are.
    Thalia: You've been busy, haven't you?
    {$playerName}: I've spoken to three people about what happened.
    Thalia: Three? Not bad.
    Thalia: Let's hear what you've learned.
    {$playerName}: Everyone remembers something strange happening near the tower.
    {$playerName}: A bright light, shaking, and then waking up here.
    Thalia: Sounds familiar.
    Thalia: I remember waking up in that graveyard, but everything before that is a blur.
    {$playerName}: There's something else.
    Thalia: Oh?
    Thalia: Don't keep me waiting.
    {$playerName}: I found a portal nearby.
    Thalia: A portal?
    Thalia: Now that's interesting.
    {$playerName}: I also went back to speak with the Lost Villager.
    {$playerName}: He remembered seeing a strange light coming from the tower before it happened.
    Thalia: Huh...
    Thalia: So the tower and that portal might be connected.
    {$playerName}: That's what he thinks.
    Thalia: Well, it's certainly more information than we had before.
    Thalia: A mysterious tower, floating islands, and a portal that leads who knows where.
    Thalia: Sounds like someone's been keeping secrets.
    {$playerName}: What do you think we should do?
    Thalia: Keep investigating, obviously.
    Thalia: But for now, you've done what I asked.
    <<set $towerInvestigationComplete = true>>
    <<complete_quest QuestManager "investigate_tower">>
    <<change_affection GameManager "characterthalia" 15>>
    Thalia: You've earned my trust.
    Thalia: A little, anyway.
    {$playerName}: I'll take that as a compliment.
    Thalia: You should.
    Thalia: I don't hand those out often.
    Thalia: Besides, someone who can uncover a secret like that might be useful around.
    {$playerName}: So we're working together now?
    Thalia: Don't get ahead of yourself.
    Thalia: But I suppose I wouldn't mind having you around.
<<else>>
    Thalia: Back already?
    Thalia: Have you learned anything useful?
    {$playerName}: I've spoken to {$towerPeopleSpokenTo} people so far.
    <<if $towerPeopleSpokenTo == 0>>
        Thalia: Nothing yet?
        Thalia: Well, answers aren't going to come knocking on your door.
        Thalia: Go talk to a few people.
    <<elseif $towerPeopleSpokenTo < 3>>
        Thalia: Good. Keep going.
        Thalia: I want to hear what three different people remember.
    <<elseif $foundTeleporter == false>>
        Thalia: Three people? Not bad.
        Thalia: But I still feel like we're missing something.
        Thalia: Keep exploring.
        Thalia: There might be something around here that explains what happened.
    <<elseif $spokeToVillagerAboutTower == false>>
        Thalia: You've found a portal?
        Thalia: Now that's something worth investigating.
        Thalia: Didn't you mention a Lost Villager earlier?
        Thalia: Maybe finding that portal will help jog his memory.
        Thalia: Go see what he knows.
    <<endif>>
    Thalia: And keep your eyes open.
    Thalia: Something about this place doesn't feel right.
<<endif>>
===
title: ThaliaRelationship
---
<<if $thaliaPositiveInteractionSeen == true>>
    Thalia: Well, if it isn't my favourite partner in crime.
    Thalia: Relax. I'm joking.
    Thalia: Mostly.
<<elseif $thaliaReceivedGem == true>>
    Thalia: Oh! {$playerName}.
    Thalia: Here to check whether I've stolen anything else?
    {$playerName}: Should I be worried?
    Thalia: Only if you've brought something shiny.
<<else>>
    Thalia: Look who it is.
    Thalia: My favourite little investigator.
    {$playerName}: Still calling me that?
    Thalia: Until you give me a reason to stop.
<<endif>>
-> Ask how she's doing
    {$playerName}: How have you been holding up?
    Thalia: Better than when I woke up in that graveyard.
    Thalia: Though that's not exactly a high standard.
    {$playerName}: Still thinking about what happened?
    Thalia: Of course.
    Thalia: But I suppose having someone else around makes things a little less miserable.
    {$playerName}: I'll take that as a compliment.
    Thalia: Don't let it go to your head.
    <<jump ThaliaRelationship>>
-> Give Thalia a Gem <<if $thaliaReceivedGem == false && has_item("gem")>>
    <<jump ThaliaGemGift>>
-> Spend some time with Thalia <<if $thaliaPositiveInteractionUnlocked == true>>
    <<jump ThaliaPositiveInteraction>>
-> Leave
    {$playerName}: I'll see you around, Thalia.
    Thalia: Try not to get into too much trouble.
    Thalia: Leave some for me.
===
title: ThaliaGemGift
---
{$playerName}: Hey, Thalia. I've got something for you.
Thalia: Oh?
Thalia: Should I be worried?
{$playerName}: I thought you might like this.
Thalia: Wait...
Thalia: Is that a gem?
{$playerName}: Yeah. I found it while exploring.
Thalia: You're willingly handing a valuable gem to a thief?
Thalia: You really are something else.
{$playerName}: Do you want it or not?
Thalia: Well, when you put it like that...
-> Give Thalia the Gem
    {$playerName}: Here. It's yours.
    Thalia: Huh...
    Thalia: You really are giving it to me.
    {$playerName}: Is that so surprising?
    Thalia: Usually when someone hands me something valuable,
    Thalia: It's because I convinced them it was a good idea.
    {$playerName}: And this time?
    Thalia: This time you did it all on your own.
    Thalia: Honestly, you're making my job far too easy.
    <<remove_item GameManager "gem">>
    <<set $thaliaReceivedGem = true>>
    <<change_affection GameManager "characterthalia" 20>>
    <<if $towerInvestigationComplete == true && get_affection("characterthalia") >= 20>>
        <<set $thaliaPositiveInteractionUnlocked = true>>
    <<endif>>
    Thalia: Jokes aside...
    Thalia: Thank you.
    {$playerName}: You're welcome.
    Thalia: Don't look so surprised.
    Thalia: Even ghosts know how to appreciate a gift.
    Thalia: I'll keep it somewhere safe.
    Thalia: And before you ask, no, you can't have it back.
    {$playerName}: I wasn't going to ask.
    Thalia: Good.
    Thalia: Because I think I'll hold onto this one.
-> Keep the Gem
    {$playerName}: Actually, I think I'll keep it for now.
    Thalia: Hah! There it is.
    Thalia: I was beginning to think you had absolutely no survival instincts.
    Thalia: Smart choice.
    Thalia: Never trust a thief with something shiny.
===
title: ThaliaPositiveInteraction
---
Thalia: Hey, {$playerName}.
Thalia: Got a moment?
{$playerName}: Sure. What's up?
Thalia: Nothing serious.
Thalia: I just wanted to ask you something.
{$playerName}: That's unusual.
Thalia: Oh, very funny.
Thalia: Keep that up and I'll start charging you for my company.
{$playerName}: What's on your mind?
Thalia: That gem you gave me...
Thalia: Why did you do it?
{$playerName}: What do you mean?
Thalia: You could've sold it.
Thalia: Or kept it for yourself.
Thalia: But instead, you gave it to someone you barely know.
-> Because I wanted to make you happy
    {$playerName}: I thought it might make you happy.
    Thalia: ...
    Thalia: You really don't know when to stop surprising me, do you?
    {$playerName}: Is that a bad thing?
    Thalia: No.
    Thalia: I suppose it isn't.
    <<if $thaliaPositiveInteractionSeen == false>>
        <<change_affection GameManager "characterthalia" 5>>
    <<endif>>
-> Because I trust you
    {$playerName}: Because I trust you.
    Thalia: Trust me?
    Thalia: You do remember what I do for a living, right?
    {$playerName}: I do.
    Thalia: Hm.
    Thalia: You're either incredibly brave or incredibly foolish.
    {$playerName}: Which one?
    Thalia: ...
    Thalia: I'll let you know when I figure it out.
    <<if $thaliaPositiveInteractionSeen == false>>
        <<change_affection GameManager "characterthalia" 5>>
    <<endif>>
-> I thought a thief would appreciate something valuable
    {$playerName}: I figured a thief would appreciate something valuable.
    Thalia: Hah!
    Thalia: Now that's an answer I can respect.
    {$playerName}: Glad you approve.
    Thalia: Careful.
    Thalia: Keep giving me things and I might start expecting them.
<<set $thaliaPositiveInteractionSeen = true>>
Thalia: Anyway...
Thalia: I just wanted to say that I appreciate it.
{$playerName}: You're welcome.
Thalia: Now, if you tell anyone I was being sentimental,
Thalia: I'll deny every word.
{$playerName}: Your secret's safe with me.
Thalia: Good.
Thalia: Maybe you really are someone I can trust.
===
